  "raw_response": "```python\nfrom collections import deque\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef solve(grid: List[List[int]]) -> List[List[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Transform the input grid according to the discovered rule:\n    - Keep all non\u2011zero cells unchanged (they form the shape).\n    - All zero cells that are reachable from the border (outside the shape) become 3.\n    - All zero cells that are not reachable from the border (i.e., interior holes\n      completely surrounded by the shape) become 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n\n    # Copy original grid for the output\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # Mark cells that are reachable from the outside (border) while staying on zeros.\n    visited = [[False] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    q = deque()\n\n    # Initialise queue with all border zero cells\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in (0, cols - 1):\n            if grid[r][c] == 0:\n                q.append((r, c))\n                visited[r][c] = True\n    for c in range(cols):\n        for r in (0, rows - 1):\n            if grid[r][c] == 0 and not visited[r][c]:\n                q.append((r, c))\n                visited[r][c] = True\n\n    # 4\u2011directional neighbours\n    dirs = [(1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1)]\n\n    while q:\n        r, c = q.popleft()\n        for dr, dc in dirs:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols:\n                if not visited[nr][nc] and grid[nr][nc] == 0:\n                    visited[nr][nc] = True\n                    q.append((nr, nc))\n\n    # Fill the grid: 3 for outside zeros, 2 for interior zeros\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 0:\n                out[r][c] = 2 if not visited[r][c] else 3\n\n    return out\n```",
  "script": "from collections import deque\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef solve(grid: List[List[int]]) -> List[List[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Transform the input grid according to the discovered rule:\n    - Keep all non\u2011zero cells unchanged (they form the shape).\n    - All zero cells that are reachable from the border (outside the shape) become 3.\n    - All zero cells that are not reachable from the border (i.e., interior holes\n      completely surrounded by the shape) become 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n\n    # Copy original grid for the output\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # Mark cells that are reachable from the outside (border) while staying on zeros.\n    visited = [[False] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    q = deque()\n\n    # Initialise queue with all border zero cells\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in (0, cols - 1):\n            if grid[r][c] == 0:\n                q.append((r, c))\n                visited[r][c] = True\n    for c in range(cols):\n        for r in (0, rows - 1):\n            if grid[r][c] == 0 and not visited[r][c]:\n                q.append((r, c))\n                visited[r][c] = True\n\n    # 4\u2011directional neighbours\n    dirs = [(1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1)]\n\n    while q:\n        r, c = q.popleft()\n        for dr, dc in dirs:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols:\n                if not visited[nr][nc] and grid[nr][nc] == 0:\n                    visited[nr][nc] = True\n                    q.append((nr, nc))\n\n    # Fill the grid: 3 for outside zeros, 2 for interior zeros\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 0:\n                out[r][c] = 2 if not visited[r][c] else 3\n\n    return out",
